day and Tuesday. So, 60 (Monday) + 45 (Tuesday) = 105 gallons in total. \n\nNext, he sells each gallon for $1.2. So, the total money made would be the total gallons multiplied by the price per gallon. That's 105 gallons * $1.2 per gallon. Let me calculate that. \n\nBreaking it down, 100 gallons * $1.2 is $120, and 5 gallons * $1.2 is $6, so adding those together gives $126. \n\nWait, is there any chance I made a mistake in the calculations? Let me check again. \n\nMonday: 4 inches * 15 gallons = 60 gallons. Correct. Tuesday: 3 inches * 15 gallons = 45 gallons. Total: 60 + 45 = 105 gallons. 105 * $1.2 = $126. Seems right. \n\nI think that's all. So the answer should be $126.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how much money James made from selling water, we start by calculating the total amount of water he collected over the two days of rain:\n\n- On **Monday**, 4 inches of rain collected **15 gallons per inch**, so:  \n  $$ 4 \\times 15 = 60 \\, \\text{gallons} $$\n\n- On **Tuesday**, 3 inches of rain collected **15 gallons per inch**, so:  \n  $$ 3 \\times 15 = 45 \\, \\text{gallons} $$\n\nTotal water collected:  \n$$ 60 + 45 = 105 \\, \\text{gallons} $$\n\nHe sells each gallon for **$1.2**, so the total money made is:  \n$$ 105 \\times 1.2 = 126 \\, \\text{\\$} $$\n\n$$ \\boxed{126} $$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "James has a rainwater collection barrel.  For each inch of rain he collects 15 gallons.  On Monday it rained 4 inches and on Tuesday it rained 3 inches.  He can sell water for $1.2 per gallon.  How much money did he make from selling all the water?", "answer": "It rained 3+4=<<3+4=7>>7 inches\nSo he collected 7*15=<<7*15=105>>105 gallons\nSo he makes 105*1.2=$<<105*1.2=126>>126 from selling the water\n#### 126", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: James has a rainwater collection barrel.  For each inch of rain he collects 15 gallons.  On Monday it rained 4 inches and on Tuesday it rained 3 inches.  He can sell water for $1.2 per gallon.  How much money did he make from selling all the water?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["126"], "solution": "126"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 7801, 702, 264, 11174, 12987, 4426, 20311, 13, 220, 1752, 1817, 17122, 315, 11174, 566, 51207, 220, 16, 20, 50122, 13, 220, 1913, 7014, 432, 435, 2627, 220, 19, 14924, 323, 389, 7589, 432, 435, 2627, 220], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 7801, 702, 264, 11174, 12987, 4426, 20311, 11, 1290, 30, 1597, 369, 1817, 17122, 315, 11174, 11, 566, 51207, 220, 16, 20, 50122, 13, 2055, 11, 358, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1753, 3015, 566, 14548, 504, 7014, 323, 7589, 11, 1221, 11047, 279, 3220, 566, 1865, 504, 11236, 429, 3015, 518, 400, 16, 13, 17]}
