\n\nThen last round: 4 matches, half of which is 2. So total is 12 + 2 = 14. Yes.\n\nAlternatively, if the problem had said \"win half of the 4 matches in the last round\", then it's 2. So total 14. So I think that is correct. Therefore, the answer should be 14. Therefore, in boxed form, \\boxed{14}.\n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{14}\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many matches Brendan won throughout the competition, we will analyze the problem step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: First Two Rounds\n\nBrendan wins **all matches** in the first two rounds. Each of these rounds had **6 matches**. Therefore, the total number of matches won in the first two rounds is:\n\n$$\n2 \\times 6 = 12 \\text{ matches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Last Round\n\nIn the last round, Brendan **wins half of the 4 matches**. \n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{2} = 2 \\text{ matches}\n$$\n\nSo, in this round, he won **2 more matches**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Total Matches Won\n\nAdding the matches won in the first two rounds and the last round:\n\n$$\n12 + 2 = 14 \\text{ matches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{14}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 