aybe not. Alternatively, maybe \"twice as many red\" as black? If that's the case, then R = 2B. Then with B = 2 (blue pens) ?\n\nWait, but then if blue pens are 2, then B would be 2 as well. Then red pens would be 4, so total pens 2 (blue) + 2 (black) + 4 (red", "source_record": {"question": "Roy has 2 blue pens. He has twice as many black and 2 less than twice as many red than black pens. How many pens does Roy have in all?", "answer": "Roy has 2 x 2 = <<2*2=4>>4 black pens.\nTwice the number of black pens is 4 x 2 = <<4*2=8>>8.\nSo, there are 8 - 2 = <<8-2=6>>6 red pens.\nTherefore, Roy has 2 + 6 + 4 = <<2+6+4=12>>12 pens in all.\n#### 12", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Roy has 2 blue pens. He has twice as many black and 2 less than twice as many red than black pens. How many pens does Roy have in all?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["12"], "solution": "12"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 11038, 702, 220, 17, 6303, 22601, 13, 1260, 702, 10917, 438, 1657, 3691, 323, 220, 17, 2686, 1091, 10917, 438, 1657, 2518, 1091, 3691, 22601, 13, 2585, 1657, 22601, 1558, 11038, 614, 304, 678, 5267, 36842, 25], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 22601, 11038, 702, 13, 88190, 11, 279, 3491, 2727, 11038, 702, 220, 17, 6303, 22601, 13, 5005, 432, 33845, 566, 702, 10917, 438, 1657, 3691, 323, 220, 17, 2686, 1091, 10917, 438, 1657, 2518, 1091, 3691, 22601, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 279, 2790, 1372, 315, 22601, 13, 6771, 752, 1438, 419]}
