t, the notebooks: 2 * $4 = $8. Correct. Pens: 2 * $1.50 = $3. So total is 8 + 3 = $11. Original money is $15. So 15 - 11 = $4. Yeah, that seems right.\n\nI don't think I made any errors here. Maybe I can verify with another method. Alternatively, maybe convert everything to dollars. But the numbers are already in dollars, so no conversion needed. Let me check if the operations are correct. 2 notebooks at 4 each: 8. 2 pens at 1.5 each: 3. 8 + 3 = 11. 15 - 11 = 4. Yep. So I think the answer is $4.00.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe amount of money Rubble will have left is \\boxed{4}.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how much money Rubble will have after purchasing his supplies, we need to first calculate the total cost of the items he needs to buy and then subtract that from the original amount of money in his pocket.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine the total number and cost of items\n\n- He needs to buy **2 notebooks** at **$4.00 each**:  \n  Cost = $4.00 × 2 = **$8.00**\n\n- He needs to buy **2 pens** at **$1.50 each**:  \n  Cost = $1.50 × 2 = **$3.00**\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the total cost of the items\n\n$$\n\\text{Total cost} = \\$8.00 + \\$3.00 = \\$11.00\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Subtract the total cost from the original money\n\nRubble has $15 in his pocket, and the total cost of the items is $11.00. Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\text{Money left} = \\$15 - \\$11 = \\$4.00\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\nThe amount of money Rubble will have left is \\boxed{4}.<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Rubble has $15 in his pocket and he needs to buy 2 notebooks and 2 pens. Each notebook cost $4.00 meanwhile each pen cost $1.50. How much money will be left from Rubble after the purchase?", "answer": "The total cost of two notebooks is $4.00 x 2 = $<<4*2=8.00>>8.00.\nThe total cost of two pen $1.50 x 2 = $<<1.5*2=3.00>>3.00.\nSo, the total amount Rubble spent for all the stuff was $8.00 + $3.00 = $<<8+3=11.00>>11.00.\nTherefore, Rubble was left off with $15.00 - $11.00 = $<<15-11=4.00>>4.00.\n#### 4", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Rubble has $15 in his pocket and he needs to buy 2 notebooks and 2 pens. Each notebook cost $4.00 meanwhile each pen cost $1.50. How much money will be left from Rubble after the purchase?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["4"], "solution": "4"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 12839, 891, 702, 400, 16, 20, 304, 806, 17822, 323, 566, 3880, 311, 3695, 220, 17, 78531, 323, 220, 17, 22601, 13, 8886, 37166, 2783, 400, 19, 13, 15, 15, 36218, 1817, 5750, 2783, 400, 16, 13], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 2055, 11, 12839, 891, 702, 400, 16, 20, 304, 806, 17822, 11, 323, 566, 3880, 311, 3695, 220, 17, 78531, 323, 220, 17, 22601, 13, 8886, 37166, 7049, 400, 19, 13, 15, 15, 11, 323, 1817, 5750, 374, 400, 16, 13, 20, 15, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477]}
