0 feet long, calculate the length of the rest of its body minus the head.\"\n\nSo, rest of its body minus the head. So, if rest of the body is (total length - head), then subtract the head. So that would be (total length - head) - head = total length - 2 * head. But maybe they want just the rest (total - head) minus head? Which would be same as total - 2*head. But let me think again. Suppose the snake is 10 feet long. Head is 1/10 of 10 = 1 foot. So, rest of its body is 10 - 1 = 9 feet. Then, rest of body is 9 feet, minus head which is 1 foot. So 9 - 1 = 8 feet. Therefore, the answer would be 8 feet? But let me check if that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, if they want total length minus twice the head, which would be 10 - 2*1 = 8. So same result. Therefore, answer is 8 feet. Therefore, boxed answer would be \\boxed{8}. Let me check once more.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the problem is phrased differently. Let me check the original problem again: \"A snake's head is one-tenth its length. If a snake is 10 feet long, calculate the length of the rest of its body minus the head.\" So rest of its body minus the head. So rest of its body is the total body minus head, so 10 - 1 = 9, then minus head, which is 9 - 1 = 8. So yes, 8 feet. Therefore, the answer is 8. I think that's it. Maybe mistranslation or something, but according to the problem, it's 8. So I think that's correct. So boxed 8.\n</think>\n\nTo solve this problem, we start by understanding the relationship between the snake's total length and its head. The problem tells us that the **head is one-tenth of the snake's length**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Find the length of the head\n\nThe snake is **10 feet long**, and the head is **one-tenth** of this length.  \n$$\n\\text{Length of the head} = \\frac{1}{10} \\times 10 = 1 \\text{ foot}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine the length of the rest of the snake's body\n\nThe rest of the snake's body is the entire length of the snake minus the head.  \n$$\n\\text{Length of the rest of the body} = 10 - 1 = 9 \\text{ feet}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the final result\n\nWe are asked to calculate the **length of the rest of the body minus the head**. So:\n$$\n\\text{Final result} = \\text{Length of the rest of the body} - \\text{Length of the head} = 9 - 1 = 8 \\text{ feet}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n$$\n\\boxed{8}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "A snake's head is one-tenth its length. If a snake is 10 feet long, calculate the length of the rest of its body minus the head.", "answer": "A snake's head is one-tenth its length, which is 1/10*10 = <<1/10*10=1>>1 foot.\nSince the snake's head is 1 foot, the rest of its body is 10-1 = <<10-1=9>>9 feet long.\n#### 9", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: A snake's head is one-tenth its length. If a snake is 10 feet long, calculate the length of the rest of its body minus the head.\nSolution:", "solutions": ["9"], "solution": "9"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 362, 25265, 594, 1968, 374, 825, 2385, 20684, 1181, 3084, 13, 1416, 264, 25265, 374, 220, 16, 15, 7541, 1293, 11, 11047, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 2732, 315, 1181, 2487, 27283, 279, 1968, 624, 36842, 25, 151645], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 419, 3491, 13, 2055, 11, 279, 3405, 374, 911, 264, 25265, 13, 576, 1968, 374, 825, 2385, 20684, 315, 1181, 3084, 11, 323, 279, 25265, 374, 220, 16, 15, 7541, 1293, 13, 1205, 1184, 311, 1477, 279, 3084, 315, 279, 2732, 315, 279, 2487, 27283, 279, 1968, 13, 88190, 11, 1077, 752, 1438, 419]}
